# Never read backend public and db/seeds/ folders

Agents must **never** read, list, search, open, or summarize files under:

- `fang-backend/public/`
- `fang-backend/db/seeds/`
- `empire-backend/public/`
- `empire-backend/db/seeds/`

(including any absolute path ending in those segments, e.g. `/Users/.../fang-backend/public/...`).

## Why

These directories hold static image assets and big data files. Paths are already exposed as opaque URL strings via API responses, `docs/api.md`, and `db/seeds/*.yml`. Reading binary/data/media trees wastes context and is disallowed by project policy.

## Cursor enforcement

- `.cursorignore` in this repo ignores `public/`
- Sibling frontend/backend repos also ignore these paths via `.cursorignore` and always-on `.cursor/rules`

## What to do instead

- Use `docs/api.md` / seed YAML for expected path strings
- Prefer API JSON fields (`avatar`, etc.)
- If an asset is missing, update seeds/docs and note the intended path — do not inspect `public/`
- If wanting to refer to a file inside db/seeds, just go with the default format and expect it to be present on runtime
